@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rgbled: <http://example.org/agora/rgb-led#> .
@prefix wokwi: <http://example.org/agora/wokwi#> .
@prefix mc: <http://example.org/agora/microcontroller#> .

<http://example.org/agora/rgb-led> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "RGB LED" ;
    rdfs:comment """One part, its own package. Four legs: three driven and one common return.""" .

rgbled:RgbLed a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf mc:Peripheral ; rdfs:label "RGB LED" ;
    wokwi:part "wokwi-rgb-led" ;
    # No wokwi:attrs stating the polarity. Which it is, is a fact about the PART SOLDERED HERE
    # and not about RGB LEDs, and the world already says it: the common leg's wire goes to
    # ground on a cathode part and to a rail on an anode one. Declaring it beside the wire that
    # determines it is how the two get to disagree.
    wokwi:pin [ mc:pinRole rgbled:RedPinRole   ; wokwi:name "R"   ] ,
              [ mc:pinRole rgbled:GreenPinRole ; wokwi:name "G"   ] ,
              [ mc:pinRole rgbled:BluePinRole  ; wokwi:name "B"   ] ,
              [ mc:pinRole rgbled:CommonPinRole ; wokwi:name "COM" ] ;
    rdfs:comment "Three driven legs and a common return, which IS now modelled — a common cathode goes to ground and a common anode to a rail, and which one it is decides whether every colour comes out as itself or as its complement. That used to be a comment in a world file saying 'check before you solder'; a checker cannot read a comment." .

rgbled:CommonPinRole a mc:PinRole ; rdfs:label "common" ;
    rdfs:comment """The shared return of all three colours. Neither a ground nor a power leg, which is exactly why it is its own role and why Wokwi calls it COM: WHICH of the two it is, is the wire's business and not the part's. Tied to ground it is a common-cathode LED and a leg driven HIGH lights; tied to a rail it is common-anode and the logic inverts.

Modelling it as ag:GroundPinRole was a small lie that only held for half the parts in the world, and it broke the moment a common-anode one was wired — the leg stopped being nameable at all, because the mapping was keyed on a role the part no longer had.""" .

rgbled:RedPinRole a mc:OutputRole ; rdfs:label "red" .
rgbled:GreenPinRole a mc:OutputRole ; rdfs:label "green" .
rgbled:BluePinRole a mc:OutputRole ; rdfs:label "blue" .
